  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know,</p><p><math><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><msup><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math> &hellip;(1)<br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> &hellip;(2)<br />From (1) and (2), we get,</p><p>&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math> .<br />Now, the diameter of the circle is <math><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math> (as the radius is <math><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math> )<br />Hence, the line passes through the center</p><p><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math></p>"
  }
